{"records":[{"id":"rrfg58k5h4","title":"Dataset of Transient HSP90 inhibition enhances sensitivity of mantle cell lymphoma to poly (ADP-ribose) polymerase (PARP) inhibitors","description":"The secondary data of Transient HSP90 inhibition enhances sensitivity of mantle cell lymphoma to poly (ADP-ribose) polymerase (PARP) inhibitors","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2022-12-15T08:16:18.015Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/rrfg58k5h4","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/rrfg58k5h4"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Chaowen","last_name":"Shi","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Poly ADP Ribose Polymerase","B-Cell Lymphoma"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"k6ws6jmwjb","title":"Real-Time Imaging of Drug-induced Trapping of Cellular Topoisomerases and Poly(ADP-ribose) Polymerase 1 at the Single-Molecule Level","description":"Original dataset for the manuscript \"Real-Time Imaging of Drug-induced Trapping of Cellular Topoisomerases and Poly(ADP-ribose) Polymerase 1 at the Single-Molecule Level\"","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2023-08-22T03:15:15.798Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/k6ws6jmwjb","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/k6ws6jmwjb"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Yilun","last_name":"Sun","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Molecular Biology","Microscopy","Chemotherapy","Poly ADP Ribose Polymerase","Topoisomerase","DNA Damage"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"xpzp3bv4ty","title":"The Lactate-NAD+ axis activates cancer associated fibroblasts by downregulating p62, Cell Reports 2022","description":"Reduced p62 levels are associated with the induction of the cancer-associated fibroblast (CAF) phenotype, which promotes tumorigenesis in vitro and in vivo through inflammation and metabolic reprogramming. However, how p62 is downregulated in the stroma fibroblasts by tumor cells to drive CAF activation is an unresolved central issue in the field. Here we show that tumor-secreted lactate downregulate p62 transcriptionally through a mechanism involving reduction of the NAD+/NADH ratio, which impaired poly(ADP-Ribose)-polymerase 1 (PARP-1) activity. PARP-1 inhibition blocked the poly(ADP-ribosyl)ation of the AP-1 transcription factors, c-FOS and c-JUN, which is an obligate step for p62 downregulation. Importantly, restoring p62 levels in CAFs by NAD+ rendered CAFs less active. PARP inhibitors, such as Olaparib, mimicked lactate in the reduction of stromal p62 levels, as well as the subsequent stromal activation both in vitro and in vivo, which suggests that therapies utilizing Olaparib would benefit from strategies aimed at inhibiting CAF activity.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2022-04-29T14:18:48.086Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/xpzp3bv4ty","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/xpzp3bv4ty"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Moscat","last_name":"Diaz-Meco","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Prostate Cancer","Microenvironment","Metabolism"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"65pfcj4j4m","title":"Protocol of CRISPR-Cas9 knockout screens for identifying ferroptosis regulators","description":"Ferroptosis, an iron-dependent programmed cell death triggered by excessive lipid peroxidation, has shown promising therapeutic potentials in human diseases. Here, we describe a protocol of a CRISPR-Cas9 loss-of-function screen to identify regulators in response to different inducers of ferroptosis. We emphasize the steps of library amplification, drug treatment, high-throughput sequencing preparation, and bioinformatics analysis using Model-based Analysis of Genome-wide CRISPR-Cas9 Knockout (MAGeCK). We also present a method to discover the regulators of ferroptosis and verify the potential targets efficiently.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2023-10-24T01:46:48.793Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/65pfcj4j4m","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/65pfcj4j4m"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Xin","last_name":"Yang","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Wei","last_name":"Gu","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["CRISPR/Cas9","Ferroptosis"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"39yjvmwk7b","title":"PARP enzyme de novo synthesis of protein-free poly(ADP-ribose), Langelier et al.","description":"Raw images for manuscript MOLECULAR-CELL-D-24-00946, \"PARP enzyme de novo synthesis of protein-free poly(ADP-ribose)\"","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2024-10-11T14:46:09.198Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/39yjvmwk7b","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/39yjvmwk7b"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Marie-France","last_name":"Langelier","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Biochemistry","Molecular Biology","Structural Biology"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"f5jtt3s8hv","title":"GCN2 is a determinant of the response to WEE1 kinase inhibition in small-cell lung cancer ","description":"Patients with small-cell lung cancer (SCLC) are in dire need of more effective therapeutic options. Frequent disruption of the G1 checkpoint in SCLC cells creates a dependency on the G2/M checkpoint to maintain genomic integrity. Indeed, in pre-clinical models, inhibiting the G2/M checkpoint kinase WEE1 shows promise in inhibiting SCLC growth. However, toxicity and acquired resistance have limited the clinical effectiveness of this strategy. Here, using CRISPR/Cas9 knockout screens in vitro and in vivo, we identified multiple factors influencing the response of SCLC cells to the WEE1 kinase inhibitor AZD1775, including the GCN2 kinase and other members of its signaling pathway. Rapid activation of GCN2 upon AZD1775 treatment triggers a stress response in SCLC cells. Pharmacological or genetic activation of the GCN2 pathway enhances cancer cell killing by AZD1775. Thus, activation of the GCN2 pathway represents a novel approach for augmenting the efficacy of WEE1 inhibitors in SCLC.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2024-06-26T09:21:15.032Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/f5jtt3s8hv","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/f5jtt3s8hv"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Alexander","last_name":"Drainas","orcid":"0000-0001-9081-9850"},{"first_name":"Julien","last_name":"Sage","orcid":"0000-0002-8928-9968"}],"funders":[],"categories":["Molecular Biology","Flow Cytometry","Western Blot"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"sxpfkty7dw","title":"Raw data related to DELTEX2 C-terminal domain recognizes and recruits ADP-ribosylated proteins for ubiquitination","description":"Crosstalk between ubiquitination and ADP-ribosylation regulates spatio-temporal recruitment of key players during DNA damage repair (DDR). The Deltex family of ubiquitin ligases (DTX1–4 and DTX3L), are characterized by a RING domain followed by a C-terminal domain (DTC) of unknown function; four Deltex proteins have other domains or partner proteins for binding poly-ADP-ribose (PAR), suggesting a role for these proteins in mediating crosstalk between ubiquitination and ADP-ribosylation. Here, we use two label-free mass spectrometry techniques to identify substrates of human DTX2 and uncover a new ADP-ribose-binding domain that facilitates PAR-dependent ubiquitination.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2020-09-10T18:20:54.757Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/sxpfkty7dw","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/sxpfkty7dw"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Syed Feroj","last_name":"Ahmed","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Lori","last_name":"Buetow","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Danny","last_name":"Huang ","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Western Blot"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"n9txt6y5cj","title":"TRABID deubiquitinase overexpression enables synthetic lethality to PARP inhibitor via prolonged retention of 53BP1 at DSB sites","description":"Here, we demonstrate that TRABID deubiquitinase (DUB) binds to 53BP1 at endogenous level and regulates 53BP1 retention at DSB sites. TRABID deubiquitinates K29-linked polyubiquitination of 53BP1 mediated by E3 ubiquitin ligase SPOP and prevents 53BP1 dissociation from DSBs, consequently inducing HR defects and chromosomal instability. Prostate cancer cells with TRABID overexpression exhibit a high sensitivity to poly (ADP-ribose) polymerase (PARP) inhibitors. This dataset include all the raw data of western blot from this project.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2023-02-27T11:33:09.418Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/n9txt6y5cj","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/n9txt6y5cj"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Jian","last_name":"Ma","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Western Blot"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"zbmchm3fz4","title":"Unrestrained poly-ADP-ribosylation provides insights into chromatin regulation and human disease Prokhorova et al.","description":"ARH3/ADPRHL2 and PARG are the primary enzymes reversing ADP-ribosylation in vertebrates, yet their functions in vivo remain unclear. ARH3 is the only hydrolase able to remove serine-linked mono(ADP-ribose) (MAR) but is much less efficient than PARG against poly(ADP-ribose) (PAR) chains in vitro. Here, by using ARH3-deficient cells, we demonstrate that endogenous MARylation persists on chromatin throughout the cell cycle, including mitosis, and is surprisingly well tolerated. Conversely, persistent PARylation is highly toxic and has distinct physiological effects, in particular on active transcription histone marks such as H3K9ac and H3K27ac. Furthermore, we reveal a synthetic lethal interaction between ARH3 and PARG and identify loss of ARH3 as a mechanism of PARP inhibitor resistance, both of which can be exploited in cancer therapy. Finally, we extend our findings to neurodegeneration, suggesting that patients with inherited ARH3 deficiency suffer from stress-induced pathogenic increase in PARylation that can be mitigated by PARP inhibition.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2021-06-10T20:34:28.357Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/zbmchm3fz4","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/zbmchm3fz4"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Ivan","last_name":"Ahel","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Biochemistry","Molecular Biology","Cell Biology","Poly ADP Ribose Polymerase"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"g3by44vhwc","title":"PARylation IP-MS data set","description":"We performed an IP reaction using specific primary antibody that recognizes poly-ADP-ribose (R&D, 4335-MC-100; RRID: AB_2572318), and performed LC-MS/MS to identidy immunopurified proteins. This dataset contains the report for this proteomic assay.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2024-06-14T20:07:57.975Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/g3by44vhwc","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/g3by44vhwc"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"曾","last_name":"昊","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Analysis of Large Data Set"],"journal_issn":[]}],"total_records":138567,"page":1,"page_size":10,"execution_time":129,"aggregations":{"data_type_stats":{"dataset":138567,"collection":0},"access_type_stats":{"open":137820,"restricted":70,"embargoed":677},"top_funders_stats":[{"id":"https://ror.org/01h0zpd94","name":"National Natural Science Foundation of China","count":22